From 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Example Author <author@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] docs: define request token format

Specify the accepted token shape so the parser and callers can agree on
the compatibility boundary.
---
 docs/request-token-format.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 docs/request-token-format.txt

diff --git a/docs/request-token-format.txt b/docs/request-token-format.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/request-token-format.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+A request token begins with the `tok_` prefix.
+The remaining characters are the token value.

From 2222222222222222222222222222222222222222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Example Author <author@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:02:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: parse request tokens

Parse the documented token form. This prevents malformed values from
being accepted by downstream callers.
---
 src/request_token.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/request_token.py

diff --git a/src/request_token.py b/src/request_token.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2222222
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/request_token.py
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+def parse_request_token(value):
+    if not value.startswith("tok_"):
+        raise ValueError("invalid token")
+    return value[4:]

